Z||000006||rockcrawl||08-09-2000||09:26 PM||||Damn, I knew I should have made a mold before I sold it!! If I ever get ahold of another UQ6 sub, I'll definately make a mold! It would be so easy (and cheap) to do. I can definately make a 6.5" sub fit in it. It seems like there would be quite a demand for them. Does anyone have one I could use to make a mold?<P>jhogans, I have a book called "The Fiberglass Repair and Construction Handbook". ISBN 0-8306-2779-0, $18.95 It is an excellent book if you want to learn how to work with the itchy stuff.<P>As I stated earlier, I don't have the time to make a bunch of them, but I could make a mold and posibly have D&R Replicars (local) turn out a bunch of them using my mold. <P><P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||08-10-2000||02:16 AM||||If anyone can do that kind of stuff, Tom can.  I know he's busy right now, but maybe it would be another project for him in the future.||||reg||1
